  "title": "Half-integral flow polynomial values",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $\\Phi(G,x)$ be the flow polynomial of a graph $G$. So for every positive integer $k$, the value $\\Phi(G,k)$ equals the number of nowhere-zero $k$-flows in $G$.\n\nConjecture $\\Phi(G,5.5) > 0$ for every 2-edge-connected graph $G$.",
